{"event":{"content":[{"additional_params":{"gemini":{"thoughtSignature":""}},"text":"I have fixed the `average` function. \n\n### Explanation of the Fix\nWhen the `count` is not positive (i.e. `count <= 0`), division by zero could occur (when `count == 0`), or signed overflow could occur (e.g. when `sum == INT_MIN` and `count == -1`). \n\nBy checking if `count <= 0` at the start of the function and returning `0`, we prevent division by zero, eliminate the risk of signed integer overflow on division, and satisfy the requirement to return 0 when there are no samples.","type":"text"}],"kind":"model_turn","model":"gemini-3.5-flash","provider":"gcp.gemini","request_id":null,"response_id":"K4e-apOqEbvxz7IPwZOlCA","turn":5,"usage":{"input_tokens":2327,"output_tokens":318,"reasoning_tokens":192,"total_tokens":2645}},"hash":"134fe31bf928080fe8f66695ccec8c04784dd13d1fa5306757fd17dbc6e9ae66","prev":"acf057b79c3659c4f03e3dabf02451b5132bc9c387061926e1b097b673c73ebd","seq":15,"ts_ms":1790871341142}
